      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/kryptopterus-vitreolus-2/",
      "html": "<p>The common glass or ghost catfish, Kryptopterus vitreolus, has been kept in numerous aquariums around the world for decades, albeit mostly under the misnomer K. bicirrhis.</p><p>A routine measure in the everyday care of the fish is to examine it regularly in the beam of a strong flashlight for possible disease. In this context, a keeper with a degree in biology discovered that under certain light incidence, the glass catfish shows a distinctly colourful iridescence. This is basically the same effect of light refraction that leads to the formation of rainbows. It is not easy to capture photographically, because the interaction of light and movement of the fish must fit exactly.</p>"
    }
